     "page": 1,
     "text": "Bentley and Sons Medical Group\nRe: Joseph Singh (DOB 02/22/2000)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI am writing this letter to provide a comprehensive medical overview of Mr. Joseph Singh, who has been under my care for a series of psychiatric issues, primarily related to a history of suicide attempts. \n\nOn November 04, 2025, Mr. Singh was seen for a follow-up regarding a suicide attempt. During this visit, his blood pressure was noted to be 128/66 mmHg, and he weighed 171 pounds. At this point, he was doing well, showing positive signs of recovery and management of his condition.\n\nEarlier, on July 17, 2025, Mr. Singh was seen again for another suicide attempt. His blood pressure was 117/65 mmHg, and his weight was 175 pounds. We have been monitoring his condition since his first suicide attempt, which occurred on November 20, 2020, making it 5.6 years ago. Despite this challenging history, Mr. Singh is currently doing well.\n\nOn March 29, 2025, Mr. Singh came in for a routine lab review. His blood pressure at that time was 116/62 mmHg, and he weighed 182 pounds. The lab results showed no significant and his condition remained stable. We continue to keep a close eye on his progress.\n\nOn December 0g, 2024, Mr. Singh presented with a back strain. His blood pressure was 131/64 mmHg, and his weight was 173 pounds. His psychiatric condition, however, remained stable and well-managed.\n\nAugust 20, 2024, saw Mr. Singh being seen for another suicide attempt. His blood pressure was 123/67 mmHg, and he weighed 180 pounds. This incident is part of a series of attempts over the past few years, with the most recent one occurring 5.6 years ago. Mr. Singh's condition has shown signs of improvement, and he is adhering to his treatment plan.\n\nOn May D2, 2024, Mr. Singh was seen for yet another suicide attempt. His blood pressure was 130/71 mmHg, and he weighed 180 pounds. Despite these challenges, his mental health condition has been managed with ongoing treatment and support.\n\nJanuary 13, 2024, Mr. Singh visited for a medication refill. His blood pressure was 125/62 mmHg, and he weighed 179 pounds. At this visit, he was doing well, and there were no immediate concerns regarding his psychiatric condition.\n\nSeptember 24, 2023, Mr. Singh was seen for a suicide attempt. His blood pressure was 129/73 mmHg, and he weighed 182 pounds. This incident occurred 5.6 years after his first documented suicide attempt, and he has since been under continuous care and monitoring.\n\nMr. Singh has been non-compliant with medications and has missed several follow-up appointments, which is concern"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "Page 7  ##\ning given his history. He has reported smoking cigarettes in the past, consuming about one pack per day, but he quit on April 28, 2016. He also consumes approximately 10 alcoholic drinks per week.\n\nSocial history includes a past history of tobacco use, which he minimized in his disclosures, and alcohol consumption averaging about 10 drinks per week. This information is important to understand full context of his medical history and lifestyle.\n\nIn summary, Mr. Singh has a significant history of suicide attempts and has been under consistent psychiatric care. While he has shown periods of stability, his non-compliance with treatment and missed appointments are areas of concern. We are committed to providing ongoing support and care to help manage his condition effectively.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Tina Mcintyre\nPsychiatry\nBentley and Sons Medical Group\n"
